<div id="apple-mdm" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="landing-page-container">
    <div purpose="landing-page-content">
      <div purpose="landing-page-hero">
        <div purpose="hero-row">
          <div purpose="page-hero-content">
            <div purpose="page-hero-headings">
              <h4>Apple Device Management</h4>
              <h1>AI-native Apple MDM for modern IT and security teams</h1>
            </div>
            <div purpose="page-hero-text">
              <p>Enroll, configure, and secure Mac, iPhone, and iPad at enterprise scale. Say what you need done, approve the change, and Fleet handles the rest. Manage Apple alongside Windows, Linux, Android, and ChromeOS in one place.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="button-row">
              <a purpose="cta-button" class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="hero-quote">
            <div purpose="hero-quote-profile-image">
              <img alt="Robbie Trencheny" src="/images/robbie-trencheny-120x120@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="quote-author-info">
              <p purpose="quote-text">“Someone’s up and running on their laptop in about 20 minutes, with the right software and the right identity groups. In Jamf that was a day or two of lost productivity.”</p>
              <p purpose="quote-author-name">Robbie Trencheny</p>
              <p purpose="quote-author-title">Head of Infrastructure and IT</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hero-logos">
          <logo-carousel></logo-carousel>
        </div>
      </div><%/* landing-page-hero */%>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h3>Traditional Apple MDM is holding IT back</h3>
          <p>Most Mac management tools were built for the desk-bound era. They make distributed Apple fleets harder to enroll, harder to audit, and harder to keep compliant.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="four-column-feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Vendor lock-in</h5>
            <p>Proprietary tools trap configurations behind GUIs, with steep renewals and limited export.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Slow, risky changes</h5>
            <p>Changes happen by hand in a console, with no review and no history. One bad profile breaks Wi-Fi for everyone.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Apple-only silos</h5>
            <p>Mac-only platforms force IT to run separate tools for Windows and Linux, with separate inventories.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Stale reporting</h5>
            <p>Periodic scans miss real-time compliance gaps that auditors and security teams need to see.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Get AI working for you</h3>
            <p>Fleet works natively with your team’s AI tools, like Claude, Copilot, or any AI harness. Say what you need done. AI proposes the change, and a person on your team approves it before it touches a device. Practice it live at a <a href="/workshops">free workshop</a> and get certified.</p>
            <div purpose="checklist">
              <p>Generate configuration profiles and DDM declarations with prompts like “Block iCloud Drive on company Macs.”</p>
              <p>Ask your Macs what’s patched and what’s compliant, and get answers in seconds.</p>
              <p>Review every change before it ships, and undo any mistake.</p>
              <p>Change Mac and <a href="/windows">Windows</a> settings together, in one request.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-demo">
            <ai-tool-graphic :hide-tool-switcher="true"></ai-tool-graphic>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="feature-with-image">
          <div purpose="feature-image">
            <img alt="A screenshot of Fleet showing Apple devices being managed at scale." src="/images/fleet-mdm-hero-1006x595@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-text">
            <h3>Manage Macs with the visibility and control modern IT teams need</h3>
            <p>Fleet is <a href="/apple">AI-native, open source Apple device management</a> built on Apple's native MDM protocol, Declarative Device Management (DDM), and Apple Business Manager. Configure, secure, and patch every Mac without giving up transparency or cross-platform support.</p>
            <div purpose="checklist">
              <p>Zero-touch enrollment through Apple Business Manager and Automated Device Enrollment.</p>
              <p>Enforce FileVault, configuration profiles, and DDM declarations with prompts like “Block iCloud Drive on company Macs.”</p>
              <p>Patch macOS, install Fleet-maintained apps, and run remediation scripts on demand.</p>
              <p>Continuously evaluate CIS Benchmarks for macOS and surface vulnerabilities in real time.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-quote">
          <p purpose="quote-text">“Before Fleet, a misconfiguration could hit every Mac in the company and be very hard to roll back safely. Not any more.”</p>
          <div purpose="quote-author-info">
            <div purpose="quote-author-image">
              <img alt="Adam Anklewicz" src="/images/adam-anklewicz-120x120@2x.png">
            </div>
            <div purpose="name-and-title">
              <p purpose="author-name">Adam Anklewicz</p>
              <p purpose="author-title">Manager, IT Systems Engineering, Thumbtack</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Built for Apple-first teams</h2>
          <p>Whether you manage 500 MacBooks or 50,000, Fleet gives Mac admins the depth Apple deserves and the cross-platform reach the rest of the business needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Apple Business Manager integration</h5>
            <p>Connect ABM to Fleet and ship MacBooks directly to employees. Devices self-enroll the first time they power on.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Zero-touch deployment</h5>
            <p>Configure devices wirelessly with Automated Device Enrollment. Apps, profiles, and bootstrap packages install during Setup Assistant.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Declarative Device Management</h5>
            <p>Use Apple's modern DDM protocol so devices self-correct drift and report status asynchronously, even on slow links.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>FileVault disk encryption</h5>
            <p>Enforce FileVault, escrow recovery keys, and verify encryption status across every Mac from one dashboard.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>macOS software and patching</h5>
            <p>Deploy Fleet-maintained apps, App Store apps, and custom packages. Self-service installs keep users moving without tickets.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Live reports for every Mac</h5>
            <p>Powered by osquery, Fleet surfaces hardware, software, and security posture in seconds, not on the next inventory cycle.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>CIS Benchmarks for macOS</h5>
            <p>Run the complete macOS CIS Benchmark out of the box. Track compliance continuously and remediate with policies.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Scripts and remediation</h5>
            <p>Run shell scripts on Macs from the Fleet UI or API. Trigger fixes automatically when a policy fails.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>iOS and iPadOS, too</h5>
            <p>Enroll iPhones and iPads in user or supervised mode. Manage profiles, apps, and lost mode from the same console.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Self-hosted, Fleet-hosted, or air-gapped</h2>
          <p>Run Fleet wherever your security and compliance teams need it, with the same features either way. Your device data stays inside your network.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-row">
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Open source core</h5>
            <p>Fleet is MIT-licensed open source. Read the code, audit how Macs are managed, and adapt it to your needs.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Run it where you want</h5>
            <p>Deploy Fleet on AWS, Azure, GCP, your own data center, or use Fleet Cloud with 100% feature parity.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>One console, every platform</h5>
            <p>See macOS, iOS, iPadOS, <a href="/windows">Windows</a>, <a href="/linux">Linux</a>, Android, and ChromeOS in one inventory and one policy engine. Set up new Windows PCs with zero touch and no Microsoft license.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>API-first by design</h5>
            <p>Every feature in the Fleet UI is available over the REST API. Integrate with Okta, Jira, Slack, Snowflake, and your SIEM.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Move off Jamf without a wipe</h5>
            <p>Apple’s built-in migration moves Macs to Fleet without a wipe, so users keep working. Fleet offers free migration support for qualifying teams.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="feature-item">
            <h5>Built with the Mac admin community</h5>
            <p>Fleet's contributors are practicing Mac admins. New macOS releases are supported on day one.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="landing-page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <h2>Apple MDM frequently asked questions</h2>
        </div>
        <div purpose="faq" class="d-flex flex-column">
          <div purpose="accordion" class="d-flex flex-column justify-content-start">
            <div purpose="accordion-body">
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header1" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body1" aria-controls="apple-faq__body1">
                  Does Fleet replace Jamf?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header1">
                  Yes. Fleet manages Macs, iPhones, and iPads with Apple’s MDM and declarative device management, and manages <a href="/windows">Windows</a>, <a href="/linux">Linux</a>, and Android from the same place. Many teams replace Jamf and the second tool they use for everything else.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header2" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body2" aria-controls="apple-faq__body2">
                  Can I move off Jamf without wiping Macs?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header2">
                  Yes. Apple’s built-in migration moves devices to Fleet without a wipe. Self-host or use Fleet cloud, with every feature either way.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header3" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body3" aria-controls="apple-faq__body3">
                  Which Apple platforms does Fleet support?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header3">
                  macOS, iOS, and iPadOS. iOS and iPadOS are supported only with MDM turned on. To learn more, check out the <a href="/docs/get-started/faq#what-host-operating-systems-does-fleet-support">supported OS versions</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header4" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body4" aria-controls="apple-faq__body4">
                  Can employees enroll personal iPhones and iPads?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header4">
                  Yes. User Enrollment with a Managed Apple Account keeps work data separate. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/enroll-byod-ios-ipados-hosts">BYOD enrollment guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header5" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body5" aria-controls="apple-faq__body5">
                  How do I deploy apps to iPhones and iPads?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header5">
                  See the guides to <a href="/guides/install-app-store-apps">installing App Store apps</a> and <a href="/guides/deploy-software-packages">deploying in-house apps</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header6" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body6" aria-controls="apple-faq__body6">
                  Can I manage Macs that aren’t in Apple Business?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header6">
                  Yes. Hosts not in Apple Business can be enrolled manually. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/apple-mdm-setup#host-isnt-in-ab">Apple MDM setup guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header7" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body7" aria-controls="apple-faq__body7">
                  Can Fleet work with Munki, Puppet, or Chef?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header7">
                  Yes, via a bootstrap package. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/setup-experience#bootstrap-package">setup experience guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div purpose="accordion-item">
                <p purpose="accordion-header" id="apple-faq__header8" style="cursor: pointer;" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#apple-faq__body8" aria-controls="apple-faq__body8">
                  Can I manage multiple Apple Business accounts?
                  <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
                </p>
                <p purpose="faq-answer" id="apple-faq__body8" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="apple-faq__header8">
                  Yes, for MSPs and subsidiaries. To learn more, check out the <a href="/guides/apple-mdm-setup#best-practice">Apple MDM setup guide</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="d-flex flex-row justify-content-start">
              <p purpose="contact-note">Have another question? <a href="/docs/get-started/faq">Read the full FAQ</a> or <a href="/contact">talk to an engineer</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
